    "jobDetail": {
      "jobDescription": "Work Arrangement & Location\nHybrid work required for the first 2-3 months (2 days per week onsite at Banqiao office). Located in Far Eastern Communication Park (near Far Eastern Hospital MRT Station).\n\nJob Overview\nThis role focuses on scaling and improving reporting systems for component, silicon, and pre-production operations. You will partner with cross-functional teams including Data Analytics, Finance, Transportation/Fulfillment, GCM, and Product Cost to deliver timely, accurate reports and uncover insights that enhance forecasting and data quality.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n● Manage logistics spending compliance and provide cost analysis and reporting to business units and cross-functional partners.\n● Lead projects to improve data quality, invoice auditing, and cost predictability for both ongoing production and new product introduction (NPI) hardware.\n● Drive process improvements and automation in cost management, analytics, and reporting, including new cost management tools and analytics solutions.\n● Collaborate with teams to analyze logistics projects and initiatives, identifying opportunities for cost savings and operational efficiency.\n\nRequired Qualifications\n● Bachelor's degree in Data Science, Operations, or related field with 5+ years of data analytics experience.\n● Experience with statistical modeling, cost simulation, financial modeling, and analysis.\n● Proficiency in reporting automation and data management.\n● Advanced SQL skills and dashboard reporting expertise.\n● Strong background in data ownership, SQL automation, audit-ready scripting, statistical analysis, billing anomaly detection, unstructured data analysis, and executive reporting.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n● Basic to intermediate Python skills and experience with data pipeline or management tools.\n● Advanced degree in a quantitative field or management consulting experience.\n● Familiarity with logistics markets and key service providers.\n● Excellent verbal and written communication skills for formal and informal presentations.\n● Ability to translate complex financial data into clear insights for stakeholders.\n",
